        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0250" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg116"/>

                <head>No. 88.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Hall</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 23,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 538.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for your information in
                    respect of previous correspondence, a copy of a letter from the secretary of the
                    Pacific Steam-ship Company, dated the 6th instant, concerning the continued
                    imposition by Costa Rica of a discriminating duty of 5 percent, against American
                    vessels in favor of those of the Spanish Central American Line.</p>
                <p>I have laid a copy of this correspondence before the Secretary of the Treasury,
                    as desired.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>










